{"kind":"text","seq":39,"text":"Done — I'll stop here with the score banked.\n\n**Best coaster this round: \"Twister\" steel twister at (62,50) — 82 pieces, 15-piece chain lift to a 30 ft-class first drop through a 60° plunge, then 5 inversions (3 vertical loops + a corkscrew turnaround + a mid-course loop) strung between six airtime camelbacks, closing with a wide banked 180 — excitement 6.99 (intensity 9.94, nausea 6.04, 58 air-time, 11 drops, similarity 0.39).**\n\nNotes for next round: intensity is the binding constraint (a 14.7 variant with high-speed s-bends scored only 2.16), and max lateral G sits at 2.99 — mostly from the corkscrew taken at full post-drop speed. Slowing that element is the most likely path to buying headroom for more inversions."}
